    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d679">

                <pb facs="0894" n="794" sameAs="frus:frus1934v02/pg794"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">882.01 Foreign Control/814b: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Consul at Geneva</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Gilbert</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1934-05-10T19:00:00-04:00">May 10, 1934—7 p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>150. For Reber. We have received word from Monrovia that Barclay is circulating a
                    statement to the effect that the Council may grant an extension of time to the
                    Liberian Government to give consideration to the League Plan. This statement is
                    apparently being used to mitigate the agitation in favor of immediate
                    acceptance. In these circumstances, <pb facs="0895" n="795" xml:id="pg795"/> we
                    think it desirable for you to suggest to the Secretariat the advisability of
                        Avenol’s<anchor n="12" xml:id="d679-f1"/> immediately sending a public
                    telegram to Monrovia reminding the Liberian Government that the Council expects
                    a definite answer for consideration at its next week’s meeting, when the League
                    will take official cognisance of the Liberian problem.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d679-f1" n="12" xml:id="d679-f1-content">
                <p>Joseph Avenol, Secretary General of the League of Nations.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
